## Authentication modes

The existing username/password mode remains supported. Kerberos/keytab authentication is also available for automation. Configure `kerberos_principal` together with the Kerberos configuration/keytab paths, or use the corresponding `FREEIPA_KERBEROS_*` environment variables.

If any Kerberos setting is configured, Kerberos takes precedence over username/password. Authentication errors in Kerberos mode are returned to the caller and never trigger a silent password fallback. Keytabs are secrets and should normally be mode `0600` and supplied by a secret store.

FreeIPA uses constrained delegation from its HTTP service to LDAP. The provider credentials therefore need a forwardable TGT; configure `forwardable = true` in `krb5.conf` or an equivalent Kerberos policy.

## Write-only enrollment passwords

`freeipa_host.userpassword_wo` requires Terraform/OpenTofu 1.11 or later. The value is `Sensitive` and `WriteOnly`: it is sent to FreeIPA but is not persisted in plan/state. `userpassword_wo_version` is persistent and must be incremented when rotating the caller-supplied enrollment password. A version change without a new write-only password fails during planning.

Legacy `userpassword`, `random_password`, and `generated_password` remain available and retain their existing stateful behavior.

